WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.901
-Welcome, welcome,
welcome, welcome to

00:00:02.901 --> 00:00:04.067
"The Tonight Show," everybody.

00:00:04.067 --> 00:00:05.801
You're here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:10.267
I went to --
I saw Harry Styles last night.

00:00:10.267 --> 00:00:12.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.734 --> 00:00:14.734
We were all there together.

00:00:14.734 --> 00:00:17.200
We all went together as a group.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.400
I was just thinking -- So, I
go, and it was unbelievable.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:20.667
I got great seats
and everything like that.

00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:22.434
It was very nice of Harry
and all that stuff.

00:00:22.434 --> 00:00:23.601
So, I went.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:27.934
And it's just hard to
look cool when you're --

00:00:27.934 --> 00:00:29.400
When you're kind of --
When you're my age

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.934
at a Harry Styles concert.

00:00:31.934 --> 00:00:33.234
And you're in the front row,

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:34.501
and people are looking at you
and stuff like that.

00:00:34.501 --> 00:00:36.701
So, like -- So, he's playing
and he's awesome.

00:00:36.701 --> 00:00:39.267
It was a great show, by the way.
Go see it. And he's good.

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:40.801
And so, I go,
"Alright, I can get into this."

00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:42.000
So, I'm like that, you know?

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.300
I'm like...
♪♪

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.634
And then I'm like,
"Oh, this is really lame."

00:00:44.634 --> 00:00:46.334
I go, "This is worse than
I normally dance."

00:00:46.334 --> 00:00:48.200
So I go,
"I'm not going to really --"

00:00:48.200 --> 00:00:50.634
So, then I started going like
this for a while.

00:00:50.634 --> 00:00:52.734
And then I was like,
"That's even weirder.

00:00:52.734 --> 00:00:53.834
I don't know what's happening."

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:56.000
Then I go,
maybe clapping was good.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.701
So, I'm like -- So, give me...
♪♪

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:01.100
Then I'm like,
"This is too much clapping."

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:03.334
I was clapping too fast.
I was like...

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:07.601
Like double-clapping.
Alright, no clap.

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:10.334
Then I go with this.
-Oh!

00:01:10.334 --> 00:01:11.634
-That's just creepy.
-Not with that.

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:12.968
-You can't do that.

00:01:12.968 --> 00:01:15.133
And then, at that point, I go,
"I'm already a meme."

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:17.300
-Right. Might as well enjoy it.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.901
-I'm just going to have fun.
And I was like, "Yeah!"

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:21.667
♪ Late night ♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:24.667
♪♪

00:01:24.667 --> 00:01:26.901
I'm in a good mood.

00:01:26.901 --> 00:01:27.901
We got blood orange here,
tonight.

00:01:27.901 --> 00:01:29.200
-Oh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:32.734
-That's right. They opened up.
They were fantastic.

00:01:32.734 --> 00:01:34.267
Also, guys, today is the --

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:35.634
officially the first day
of fall.

00:01:35.634 --> 00:01:36.667
Come on!
-Oh!

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:38.400
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.167
Come on, fall.
-That's why I'm in a good mood.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:42.634
Everyone is talking about this.

00:01:42.634 --> 00:01:44.000
Last night,
former president Trump

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:46.901
was interviewed by Sean Hannity
on Fox News.

00:01:46.901 --> 00:01:48.434
And when Hannity
brought up Trump's claim

00:01:48.434 --> 00:01:51.467
that he declassified the
documents found at Mar-a-Lago,

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:53.534
Trump gave a very
interesting explanation.

00:01:53.534 --> 00:01:54.601
Take a look at this.

00:01:54.601 --> 00:01:55.801
-Is there a process?

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:57.167
What was your process
to declassify?

00:01:57.167 --> 00:02:00.067
-There doesn't have to be
a process, as I understand it.

00:02:00.067 --> 00:02:01.901
You know, there's different --
People say different things.

00:02:01.901 --> 00:02:03.567
But, as I understand,
there doesn't have to be --

00:02:03.567 --> 00:02:05.267
If you're the
President of the United States,

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:08.334
you can declassify just by
saying, "It's declassified,"

00:02:08.334 --> 00:02:09.667
even by thinking about it.

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:19.400
-Hannity was like,
"Oh, I get it.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:20.601
You're going to plead insanity.

00:02:20.601 --> 00:02:23.534
Okay, now it's making sense."

00:02:23.534 --> 00:02:25.734
Meanwhile, Ron DeSantis
was watching at home going,

00:02:25.734 --> 00:02:26.801
"Well, I guess
we've got to start

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:28.100
printing those campaign posters.

00:02:28.100 --> 00:02:29.534
Here we go."

00:02:29.534 --> 00:02:32.400
I felt like he was this close to
using the word "abracadabra."

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.300
Did you --
When Trump was talking.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.567
Trump also suggested
a pretty interesting theory

00:02:36.567 --> 00:02:39.300
on why the FBI searched
his house in the first place.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.601
Listen to this.

00:02:40.601 --> 00:02:43.000
-Because of what they did,
the severity of the FBI

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:46.801
coming and raiding Mar-a-Lago,
were they looking for the

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:48.934
Hillary Clinton e-mails
that were deleted?

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:50.801
But they are around someplace.

00:02:50.801 --> 00:02:52.434
Were they looking for the --
-Wait, wait.

00:02:52.434 --> 00:02:54.234
You're not saying you had it.
-No, no.

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:55.734
They may be saying --

00:02:55.734 --> 00:02:57.934
They may have thought
that it was in there.

00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:04.234
-At that point, even QAnon
people were like,

00:03:04.234 --> 00:03:05.968
"Okay, that conspiracy seems
a little nuts.

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:08.367
That's a little much for us."

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:09.501
You've got to give Trump
credit, though.

00:03:09.501 --> 00:03:11.200
He knows how to say
something so crazy

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.000
that it actually makes
the last crazy thing he said

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.267
seem normal.

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:15.767
You know, right?
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:17.901
Trump had a lot to say about
the search of Mar-a-Lago,

00:03:17.901 --> 00:03:19.767
including something
the FBI took from him.

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:20.901
Watch this.

00:03:20.901 --> 00:03:23.834
-They took a lot.
I think they took my will.

00:03:23.834 --> 00:03:25.901
I found out yesterday.
I said, "Where is it?"

00:03:25.901 --> 00:03:28.033
-Am I in it?
-I think they took my will.

00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:29.100
That could cause
a lot of problems.

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.167
-I know.

00:03:32.501 --> 00:03:34.167
-The FBI was like, "Oh,
you mean the piece of paper

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:35.667
with the Sharpie treasure map?

00:03:35.667 --> 00:03:37.968
Yeah, we did --"

00:03:37.968 --> 00:03:39.567
A minute later,
Melania handed it back

00:03:39.567 --> 00:03:41.734
and was like, "Sorry,
I was just checking something.

00:03:41.734 --> 00:03:43.267
"We're all good."

00:03:43.267 --> 00:03:45.601
Switching gears,
tonight on Amazon,

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:47.968
there was another
Thursday night football game.

00:03:47.968 --> 00:03:51.033
And, apparently, Amazon -- Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:51.033 --> 00:03:54.534
Apparently, Amazon has a policy
not to show ads for alcohol,

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:56.367
which means there are no
beer commercials

00:03:56.367 --> 00:03:57.834
during their football games.

00:03:57.834 --> 00:03:59.734
Yeah. I don't know why
Amazon does that,

00:03:59.734 --> 00:04:01.200
because drunk people
ordering stuff

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:03.901
on Amazon is
90% of their business.

