00:05:49.667 --> 00:05:50.968
-Some entertainment news.

00:05:50.968 --> 00:05:53.701
A new "Star Wars" show, "Andor,"
just came out on Disney+.

00:05:53.701 --> 00:05:55.033
It's getting great reviews.

00:05:55.033 --> 00:05:57.968
And I saw that the show
introduces a new droid character

00:05:57.968 --> 00:06:01.868
named B2EMO.

00:06:01.868 --> 00:06:03.467
Can we take a look at B2EMO?

00:06:05.901 --> 00:06:09.267
Honestly, he doesn't really
look that emo.

00:06:09.267 --> 00:06:11.267
Can we see some clips of him
from the show?

00:06:11.267 --> 00:06:14.267
-It's not a phase.
It's who I am.

00:06:14.267 --> 00:06:16.767
Security confiscated
my wallet chain

00:06:16.767 --> 00:06:18.968
at the My Chemical Romance show.

00:06:18.968 --> 00:06:22.033
They're not cigarettes,
Dad, they're cloves.

00:06:22.033 --> 00:06:24.901
And I'm 18, so leave me alone.

00:06:24.901 --> 00:06:26.567
Has anyone seen my

00:06:26.567 --> 00:06:28.734
"Nightmare Before Christmas"
beanie?

00:06:28.734 --> 00:06:31.133
Just pick me up
at the mall at 10:00

00:06:31.133 --> 00:06:33.267
and please don't embarrass me.

00:06:33.267 --> 00:06:35.734
This whole star system
is bull[bleep]

00:06:35.734 --> 00:06:37.434
-Oh, my God.
That was interesting.

00:06:37.434 --> 00:06:38.667
Now I get it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:38.667 --> 00:06:40.701
-Wow!
-I get it.

00:06:42.100 --> 00:06:43.400
Some more entertainment news.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:46.100
Tomorrow, "Avatar"
will be re-released in theaters

00:06:46.100 --> 00:06:47.501
all across the country.

00:06:47.501 --> 00:06:49.334
The movie originally
came out in 2009.

00:06:49.334 --> 00:06:50.567
That was a long time ago.

00:06:50.567 --> 00:06:52.267
Higgins, do you remember
where you were when you --

00:06:52.267 --> 00:06:54.200
back in 2009,
when you first saw "Avatar"?

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.834
-Oh, yeah, of course.

00:06:55.834 --> 00:06:58.334
I was dancing to "Boom Boom Pow"
by the Black Eyed Peas...

00:06:58.334 --> 00:06:59.434
-Uh-huh.

00:06:59.434 --> 00:07:00.968
-...when my friend, the Octomom,

00:07:00.968 --> 00:07:04.167
texted me the "Avatar" trailer
on my BlackBerry Storm.

00:07:04.167 --> 00:07:06.901
And as a thank-you,
I poked her on Facebook.

00:07:06.901 --> 00:07:08.467
-Oh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:10.767 --> 00:07:12.734
-Yo, I still remember
where I was

00:07:12.734 --> 00:07:14.267
when I found out about "Avatar."

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:19.367
I was hanging out with my BFFs,
Taylor Lautner and Susan Boyle.

00:07:19.367 --> 00:07:21.868
And we were
ghost-riding the whip

00:07:21.868 --> 00:07:24.534
when Susan starts telling me
how good "Avatar" is.

00:07:24.534 --> 00:07:27.567
So, I told her, "Susan Boyle,
I'mma let you finish,

00:07:27.567 --> 00:07:29.834
but 'Sisterhood of
the Traveling Pants 2'

00:07:29.834 --> 00:07:31.400
is the best movie of the year."

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:33.968
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah.
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:33.968 --> 00:07:35.200
You want to know where I was

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:36.767
when I first heard about
"Avatar"?

00:07:36.767 --> 00:07:39.534
I was doing a flash mob with
Snooki, JWoww,

00:07:39.534 --> 00:07:42.467
and The Situation's cousin,
The Circumstance.

00:07:42.467 --> 00:07:44.834
And when we realized
we all forgot to water

00:07:44.834 --> 00:07:48.033
our FarmVille crops,
so we drove to my place

00:07:48.033 --> 00:07:49.767
in my Nissan Cube
while blasting

00:07:49.767 --> 00:07:52.601
the "Glee" soundtrack,
because we're big Gleeks.

00:07:52.601 --> 00:07:55.367
And I heard an ad
for "Avatar" on the radio

00:07:55.367 --> 00:07:58.667
while Snooki was asking me if I
was Team Edward or Team Jacob.

00:07:58.667 --> 00:08:04.133
-Man, 2009 was a different time.

00:08:04.133 --> 00:08:08.067
-2009?
Mine was from this morning.

00:08:11.067 --> 00:08:14.234
-Hey, guys, I read that
battery-powered planes

00:08:14.234 --> 00:08:16.334
are gaining traction
among major airlines.

00:08:16.334 --> 00:08:18.667
They're set to be
in the air by 2028.

00:08:18.667 --> 00:08:19.834
Yeah, battery-powered planes.

00:08:19.834 --> 00:08:21.267
Actually, they've been
around for a while.

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:25.334
In fact, Spirit's entire fleet
runs on four AAA batteries.

00:08:27.167 --> 00:08:28.834
It's true.

00:08:28.834 --> 00:08:30.234
I heard about
a woman in Washington

00:08:30.234 --> 00:08:31.701
who allegedly stole a car
and didn't have

00:08:31.701 --> 00:08:32.767
a great getaway plan.

00:08:32.767 --> 00:08:33.834
Check this out.

00:08:33.834 --> 00:08:35.300
-If you plan to steal a car,

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:37.567
don't drive into
freshly poured concrete.

00:08:37.567 --> 00:08:39.334
Lakewood police say
the person who tried to

00:08:39.334 --> 00:08:41.834
make it out with this
Mini Cooper did just that.

00:08:41.834 --> 00:08:44.434
They got out and tried to run
but were arrested anyway.

00:08:44.434 --> 00:08:45.734
Police say the driver was

00:08:45.734 --> 00:08:47.934
holding a bottle of whiskey
at the time.

00:08:47.934 --> 00:08:51.300
-Yeah, you didn't need to
tell us that last part.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:53.834
We assumed. Guys, get this.

00:08:53.834 --> 00:08:55.334
Under a new law in California,

00:08:55.334 --> 00:08:57.534
employers will
soon be banned from screening

00:08:57.534 --> 00:08:59.400
employees for marijuana.

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:02.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah. That's right.

00:09:02.300 --> 00:09:05.167
Employers will no longer be able
to drug-test people.

00:09:05.167 --> 00:09:07.701
But if you ask me, they're still
trying to find ways around it.

00:09:07.701 --> 00:09:09.133
Here are some of the questions
that they're asking

00:09:09.133 --> 00:09:10.200
on the job application.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:11.334
First up, it says...

00:09:17.467 --> 00:09:19.734
You know what I'm saying?

00:09:19.734 --> 00:09:20.834
Next up, it says...

00:09:27.501 --> 00:09:28.667
-Okay.

00:09:28.667 --> 00:09:32.601
-So I'm thinking...
After that, it says...

00:09:42.234 --> 00:09:43.334
Next, it asks...

00:09:56.334 --> 00:09:58.067
-Whoa!

00:09:58.634 --> 00:09:59.834
-And, finally, it asks...

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:06.400
-Whoa!

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:09.200
-Just interesting.
I'm just saying, they're tough.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:10.367
Guys, did you see this?

00:10:10.367 --> 00:10:12.133
Residents of Salt Lake City
have reported

00:10:12.133 --> 00:10:15.534
hearing strange music
coming from the sewers.

00:10:15.534 --> 00:10:17.300
Yeah, strange music,
as opposed to

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:21.200
the totally normal music usually
heard coming from the sewers.

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:22.367
Finally, a wedding reception
in New Jersey

00:10:22.367 --> 00:10:25.734
had to be relocated
after the floor caved in

00:10:25.734 --> 00:10:27.234
while people were dancing.

00:10:27.234 --> 00:10:29.934
People showed up at the E.R.
like, "Hi.

00:10:29.934 --> 00:10:31.234
I'm here for the
Freedman wedding."

00:10:31.234 --> 00:10:33.601
Yeah. I'm pretty sure it's the
first wedding with

00:10:33.601 --> 00:10:35.334
an open bar and an open floor.

00:10:35.334 --> 00:10:36.467
We have a great show.

